==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
{{proto|Germanic|mēnōþ-|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|mēnōt-|month, moon|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|monath|mōnath}}, Old Saxon {{term|manuð|mānuð|lang=osx}} (Dutch {{term|maand|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term|manod|mānōd|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Monat|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|manaðr|mānaðr|lang=non}} (Danish {{term|Måned|lang=da}} Swedish {{term|månad|lang=sv}}), Gothic {{term|𐌼𐌴𐌽𐍉𐌸𐍃|tr=menoþs|sc=Goth}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/ˈmoːnaθ/|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
